                "reviews": [
                  {
                    "author": "Javad Ghalambor",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": "The ambience is beautiful, and the interior design stands out. The combination of white and blue colors creates a bright, elegant atmosphere and makes the space feel much more spacious.\nThe service is good and attentive. At times, I felt that the staff were watching customers a bit too closely, which made me feel slightly under surveillance. However, I believe this comes from their desire to ensure customer satisfaction, especially as a new restaurant.\nThe food is fresh, flavorful, and well-prepared. Overall, it was a pleasant dining experience, and I would recommend giving it a try if you're visiting Mall of Asia.",
                    "published": "2 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "Nidhi Poojary",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "Absolutely loved this place! The quality of the ingredients and less oil made the dishes  feel fresh and light. The cocktails were phenomenal. The pizza  crust was airy with the perfect texture. I also appreciated how generous they were with the burrata. The service was also great.  Definitely will be back.",
                    "published": "a month ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "CINDY DSILVA",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "We girls had a wonderful time here. The staff was courteous, well spoken and helpful. The ambience was lovely. The place was clean.\n\nThe food was yum. The list of items we ordered are in the photos. We loved all the items. Each of them had their respective flavours. The Alfredo sauce was what I enjoyed the most.\n\nNow a days it is difficult to find the right flavours in Italian dishes. I almost stopped having pasta in India due to the various ways in which restaurants prepare it here. But this restaurant is really good for Italian dishes, with the right cheeses and the oomph in the flavours. I'm a hardcore non vegetarian but I even loved the veg lasagne for the first time 😄\n\nDefinitely going there again! With the family.",
                    "published": "a month ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "Rahul Unnikrishnan",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "A solid Italian restaurant arriving in Bangalore with a bang! The Interiors is very nice and welcomes you in a pleasant way. The food menu js extensive. We tried the chicken fratiti, garlic break and a chicken pizza. All dishes were extremely tasty. The garlic bread was so fresh and smelling great. The chicken fratiti with its peri peri seasoning was a fun yet filling starter to have. The pizza was light, rich in flavour and tasty. We gobbled up the food quite fast. Lastly tried their Tiramisu which I loved. Service was friendly and quick!\nWe will be back soon to try more dishes as well as their drinks!",
                    "published": "2 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "Avinash Venkataraman",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "Visited in May 2026, just ten days after they opened for customers. This situated bang opposite Inox Megaplex on 3rd floor of the Mall\nOf Asia.\n\nThe staff is very welcoming. It was a busy Saturday afternoon but the service was prompt and earnest.\n\nWe tried the Siciliana Sour ( Limoncello and Gin ) , which was quite refreshing. The Passionfruit melodia mocktail was a tad sweet but nice. The edible Pasta straw idea was cool !\n\nOur small plates choices were Roasted sweet potato and the Sicilian Pizza sfincione, which was absolutely heavenly ( pizza without cheese but loaded with veggies !).\n\nFor the main we tried the Canneloni Florentine, which was beautifully done. Rich filling of spinach and ricotta and delectably done. The Tres Leches ( mango) was decadent.\n\nOverall it was a wonderful experience and I look forward to coming back and trying more items. A welcome addition to Italian fine dining cuisine in North Bangalore.\n\nLoved the blue theme!",
                    "published": "2 months ago"
                  }
                ],
