              {
                "author": "Sakshi Joshi",
                "rating": 3,
                "text": "Tucked right next to Ulsoor Lake, this café has such a calm, peaceful vibe — perfect for coffee lovers who want to slow down and actually enjoy their cup.\nThe best part is that it’s not crowded, so you can sit comfortably, work, read, or just relax without feeling rushed. The staff is genuinely warm and welcoming, which makes the whole experience even nicer.\n\nParking can be a little tricky since there’s only limited space, but once you step inside, the lovely ambience, greenery, and soothing lake-side feel make it totally worth it.\n\nOverall, great coffee, great vibes, and a beautiful, cozy setting. Definitely a must-visit if you’re around Ulsoor and love discovering peaceful cafés.\n\nP.S. : This is only for coffee lovers. They don't have tea, juices, mocktails,  etc",
                "published": "6 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Deepanshu Sharma",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "I recently stumbled upon this coffee shop near Ulsoor Lake, and I was thoroughly impressed by the exceptional taste and quality of their coffee. I highly recommend this place to anyone looking for a great coffee experience.",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Sai Singh Rajput",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "6oz is by far the best coffee station in town, the staff here are really kind\nfriendly and polite, they explained the types of coffees to try. If you guys are coffee enthusiast. A must visit place.\nWe are coming back soon, until then keep brewing;)",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "SuriFied",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Came to Six Ounce Coffee and Roasters for a coffee meetup with my travel crew, and honestly, it was awesome.\n\nThe whole place is spotless—seriously clean—and the atmosphere is super chill. I stuck with a classic cappuccino, and it was perfectly smooth and rich. My friends were raving about the variety; they tried a couple of their cold coffee options and loved them.\n\nFood-wise, everything was great! We grabbed a ridiculously flaky croissant to share. The savory sandwich selection looked tempting (I need to come back for that cream bun!). What really stood out was the staff. They’re genuinely friendly staff who know their stuff. A huge thanks to the barista   Definitely recommend this spot if you're looking for quality coffee and good vibes!",
                "published": "9 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Aamir Cassanno",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "An amazing experience of being to this cafe! I would recommend to try their Café Bombon once. The place is calm and cozy 😊",
                "published": "2 months ago"
              }
