            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "Mitika Kaushik",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "Such an elite-class cafe! Every single thing we ordered tasted amazing. I absolutely loved their mushroom toast on white bread, as well as their Biscoff shake. The egg sandwich was a little bit off, but everything else was spectacular.\n\nThe ambience is great, and they have a lovely collection of books, so you can grab a coffee, read, and just enjoy the vibe. They offer both indoor and outdoor seating areas, and both are really nice. They even have an open pizza counter!\n\nThe staff is incredibly warm and friendly. You can easily book a table through Zomato District or Swiggy Dineout.",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "髙橋一颯",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "I had such an amazing experience at Roastea - Curated Coffee And Tea Artisans!!\n\nI mentioned that I’m really into coffee, and they were incredibly kind and welcoming — honestly went way beyond what I expected.\n\nBig thanks to Carthik for making this opportunity happen, and especially to Nithish — he took the time to explain everything about the coffee in such a friendly and easy-to-understand way. It turned into a really special and memorable experience for me!!\n\nAlso, everything else was great too — the pasta and croissants were delicious, and the overall vibe of the place (both indoor and outdoor seating) was super nice and relaxing.\n\nDefinitely one of the best café experiences I’ve had. Highly recommend!!",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Akil Narayana",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "Been to Roastea multiple times, and it’s consistently delivered — the food rarely disappoints. That said, this time the Shakshuka was a bit of a letdown.\n\nThe Caprese Croissant Sandwich remains an all-time favourite — easily one of the best things on their menu. Their coffee is excellent, and the chocolate brownie and croissants are equally worth trying.\n\nIt’s definitely on the pricier side for a café, but if you book through platforms like District or Dineout, the discounts make it feel much more reasonable.\n\nValet parking is a nice touch, although it’s usually not available on weekdays until early evening.\n\nWould I recommend it? Absolutely. Just one tip — don’t pay ₹200 for a filter coffee or masala chai… that’s basically daylight robbery :P",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Sakshi Sharma",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Handkerchief pasta at Roastea lives up to the hype — silky, delicate sheets, made in-house. Went peri-peri and it brings serious heat, balanced by pesto-mozzarella and basil. The Espresso Champagne is a fun pairing and looks great in the glass.\n\nBig shoutout to Kamlesh for the service — attentive, great recommendations, made the visit.\n\nWill be back for the pumpkin version.",
                "published": "2 weeks ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Vallari Pejathaya",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Loved the new protein menu at Roastea. The Caribbean Jack was genuinely refreshing tropical, creamy, and surprisingly balanced while still packing good protein content by Yoga bar pea protein. We also tried the avocado toast and blueberry parfait, and both complemented the meal really well. The presentation, ambience, and overall experience made healthy eating feel indulgent rather than restrictive. Definitely worth trying if you’re looking for protein-rich options that actually taste good",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              }
            ],
