            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "K Ash",
                "rating": 3,
                "text": "This cozy roastery in Jayanagar focuses primarily on their coffee menu, with a small selection of food items available. The space is intimate and perfect for coffee enthusiasts looking for a quiet spot.\n\nI tried their coffee and matcha, though both didn’t quite meet my expectations - the matcha lacked depth & flavour, and the coffee was decent but not particularly memorable. The croissants could have been flakier, and the sandwich was fairly average.\n\nThis café caters specifically to coffee lovers, so if you’re not particularly into coffee, you might find the menu options somewhat limited.\n\nIt’s a nice neighborhood spot for those who appreciate a dedicated coffee focus, though there’s room for improvement in execution.",
                "published": "6 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "maithili josalkar",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Mocha with oat milk and a light roast pour over - both of them one of them best ones we have had in the city.\n\nWe also purchased their beans since they’ve a roastery also.\n\nAlso would really like to appreciate the skill with which pour overs are made here - the bloom was excellent.\n\nLimited pastries but that’s ok - the coffee is killer",
                "published": "3 weeks ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Punam",
                "rating": 3,
                "text": "Ordered Iced latte and orange cake.\nCoffee was 3/5 (the caffeine wasn’t strong)\nDessert was 3.5/5 (wasn’t very flavourful)\n\nAmbience: 4/5\nService:4/5\n\nOverall a decent experience.",
                "published": "5 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Nabanita Goswami",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "I’ve spent a few afternoons at Groundup, Jayanagar and here’s a breakdown of what to order, what’s amazing and what makes this cafe truly special on the coffee map of Blr\n\nWhat to Order\n- Cappuccino (they have two types of espresso blends, select one that suits your palate)\n- Cold Brew\n- Hot Chocolate\n- Experimental Brew (!!!) the baristas will whip up something new on your demand\n- Matcha Latte (absolutely creamy, smooth)\n\nVibes 4.5/5\n- Ground Up feels like that lovely friend you want to spend a slow Sunday with. Small, cozy, with tasteful décor and greenery of Jayanagar around. Great natural light, warmer dark tones, and a peaceful hum. The staff is 💯special mention to Salman and Faizal.\n\np.s. the cafe has limited seating; you might want to give up your seat for the next customer, especially on weekends. I’ve never ordered food there, so no comments on this.\n\nHighlights\n- ground up roasts their own beans, sourced from salawara estate. They always have experimental lots so you’ll never get bored\n- the menu is ✨curated✨ you won’t find an overwhelming list, just quality.\n- this cafe will become your fav quickly because of the smell of freshly ground coffee when you walk in, the ambience and the friendly staff.",
                "published": "8 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Arnav Kumar",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Had such a wonderful experience at this café! I ordered a hazelnut latte and a cappuccino, and both were absolutely delightful. The hazelnut latte had a perfectly balanced nutty sweetness that complemented the coffee beautifully, while the cappuccino was rich, smooth, and expertly brewed with just the right amount of foam.\nWhat truly stood out was the aroma—it filled the entire café with this comforting, inviting scent of freshly ground coffee that instantly put me in a good mood. The taste was just as impressive as the smell: deep, flavorful, and clearly made with high-quality beans. It’s the kind of place where you want to sit back, relax, and savor every sip. Definitely a café I’ll be coming back to!\n\nPS: the photo is of the Mocha and cappuccino, which is of the second visit and was really good as well",
                "published": "7 months ago"
              }
            ],
