            "phone": "(514) 325-7888",
            "editorialSummary": "From a height of 60 meters, this wheel offers 360° views over Montreal & the St Lawrence River.",
            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "diptimayee jena",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Here’s a polished version of your travel experience that reads naturally:\n\nAfter visiting the Old Montreal Port, we headed to La Grande Roue de Montréal, the famous Ferris wheel. Since there wasn’t much of a crowd, we bought our tickets directly from the counter, although buying them online is slightly cheaper.\n\nWe waited for about 15 minutes before our turn. The ride turned out to be one of the best experiences of my trip. Even though I’m afraid of heights, the Ferris wheel moves so slowly and smoothly that I didn’t feel scared at all. We visited in the evening, and the views of Montreal from the top were absolutely beautiful.\n\nAfter the ride, we treated ourselves to some ice cream, which was the perfect way to end the visit. Our kid loved it, and we enjoyed it just as much. It was a wonderful family experience that I would highly recommend to anyone visiting Montreal.",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Madison Mitchell",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "This was an excellent family friendly activity! We did a VIP experience and, other than having the glass floor, I'm not sure it was entirely necessary as everything was walkup and the regular cabins looked very comfortable. We went around 3 times and got wonderful views of the city and surrounding area. Definitely worth doing!! The little cafe/ice cream parlor is nice for visiting right after the experience.",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Khj_afsaneh Af1358",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "We come to La Grande Roue de Montréal almost every year, and it’s always one of our favorite experiences in the city. The views of Old Montreal, the river, and the skyline are absolutely beautiful, especially on a clear day.\n\nThis visit was even more special because we were able to bring our dog with us. We really appreciated how pet-friendly the experience was, and it made our family outing complete.\n\nAnother great feature is that you can play your own music inside the cabin, which makes the ride even more fun and personal.\n\nThe cabins are clean, comfortable, and spacious, and the ride is smooth and relaxing. We look forward to coming back again next year!",
                "published": "2 weeks ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "nerzhar kumar",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Visited with my wife during our trip and it was one of the highlights of our visit. We booked the VIP experience, which gave us access to a private cabin with seating for four. It felt very comfortable and offered a more intimate experience compared to a regular ride.\n\nWe went around 8.50pm in June and were treated to beautiful, panoramic sunset views of the city. The ride lasted for approximately 20min, which was about three full rotations.\n\nDespite visiting during a popular time, the wait was surprisingly short-only around 15 minutes. The area around the wheel is well maintained, and there are plenty of amenities nearby.\n\nIf you're visiting Montreal, especially as a couple, I would definitely recommend timing your ride around sunset.",
                "published": "2 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Ian Ellis",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "What a beautiful way to see Montreal. We went to go during the day but unfortunately it wasn’t operating so we returned at night. I think we chose the right time of day . The views are exceptional with the city all illuminated. Good value at around £35 for 2 adults. Well recommended",
                "published": "2 months ago"
              }
            ],
