              {
                "author": "Aditi D.",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "We just headed in for a quick bite but stayed for the absolute amazing food! The pasta was absolutely delicious, but the pizza genuinely took our breaths away.\nDefinitely check out their cocktail section as well, because they became the highlight of our night out. I’d love to visit again and try different dishes, but the food we did eat was absolutely stunning.\nBonus points for us as the founder was right there, managing everything from the kitchen to the dining floor. What a treat for us to be able to see her in action!",
                "published": "2 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Sarb Kaur",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "I recently tried this fantastic Italian restaurant, and if you’re an Italian food lover, it’s a must-visit! The ambiance is sophisticated and inviting, making it perfect for a cozy meal. The food? Amazing! And the service is top-notch.\n\nI went for the Passionfruit Chia Iced Tea, Casa Misu (Tiramisu dessert), and Tortellini Carbonara pasta — and loved every bite (or sip!) of them. If Italian cuisine is your thing, you should definitely check this place out.🥰",
                "published": "5 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Paras Chandna",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Casa Pasta bar is a lovely place to try some Italian food. This place is very cozy and has really warm vibe. The staff is very polite,and adds to the overall great experience.\nAnd ofcourse the best thing is their pasta.\nMust try\nCharcoal Mafaldine Truffle\n\nJust a suggestion,\nI tried a basil ravioli (chef's special that day), add this to your permanent menu..",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Raghav Sood Magic",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "ate at Casa last night. getting a res was easy, the staff are cordial and warm which is always good. started my meal with a glass of rosé and the prawns which were good. Followed by the chicken and mushroom ravioli which was confusing, the raviolis were too big and the sauce was too heavy. but the lamb ragu with the pappardelle was quite delicious. will definitely come again and try more!",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "anagh singh",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Recently visited this authentic Italian, aesthetically beautiful cafe in hauz khas . I loved everything about this place..from ambience to food, the staff was also very helpful and kind. Tried 3 dishes there and loved all of them. Finally i found a place which servers better pasta than big chill. The tiramisu was okiesh , nothing too fancy but definitely worth a try. I highly recommend this place for authentic Italian food. Definitely wanna visit here again..",
                "published": "7 months ago"
              }
