            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "Bikash Singh",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Had a wonderful dining experience! The Japanese and Chinese food was delicious, with great taste and quality. The service was excellent, and the entire staff was warm, friendly, and attentive. A special thanks to Sanjana for her outstanding hospitality and cheerful attitude—she made our visit even more enjoyable. Highly recommended, and I’ll definitely be coming back!",
                "published": "4 weeks ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Mohammed Javed",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "We visited Nasi n Mee on Covent Road around 10:30 pm, and the restaurant was surprisingly empty. Coming to the food, it was exceptional overall. I ordered the Nasi Goreng Mix (chicken and prawn), which was flavourful and well-balanced. The Tempura Maki Roll was nice and crispy, with a good texture and taste. We also tried the prawn crackers with dips, and I especially loved the Vietnamese chilli dip. It was damn spicy and hot, but in a very addictive way. The Sambal Fried Rice was decent, but not something that stood out as “wow” compared to the other dishes. The service was very good attentive, polite, and quick despite the late hour.\n\nOverall - Great service, flavourful food, and definitely worth trying if you enjoy Asian flavours.",
                "published": "6 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Elton Hiew",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "If you are looking to try authentic Malaysian or Singaporean food, this is definitely the place to visit for a true taste of home. The dishes were incredibly authentic and closely resembled what you would find in Malaysia and Singapore.\n\nI tried their Xiao Long Bao, which was made and steamed to perfection. It was even better than some of the Chinese restaurants back home!\n\nThe service from the staff was excellent as well. Special kudos to the lady at the entrance, who made me feel very welcome and thoughtfully suggested that I wait in the café instead of outside while waiting for my Uber. Such a small gesture and friendly conversation truly left a positive impression on me.",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Shruti Thakur",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Went to Nasi and Mee for lunch and honestly… the vibe was vibing ✨\n\nSuch a solid spot if you’re craving Pan-Asian & Thai — the menu has so many options, it’s lowkey hard to pick. But everything we tried? Hit. 🤌🏻 a star place fr.\n\nFood on my table:\n🥤 N&M Ice Blended Milo\n🍉 Fresh Watermelon Juice\n🥟 Roasted Pepper Chicken Dimsums\n🔥 Flaming Salmon Sushi\n🍜 Yaki Udon tossed in Yakitori sauce\n🍲 Tantanmen Chicken Ramen – rich broth, proper comfort bowl\n🍫 Chocolate Banana Spring Roll\n\nOverall: great food, great vibe, and definitely a place I’d go back to when the cravings hit 🫶🏻",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "KpD_007",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Visited for lunch, had chicken karaage, Hawaiian Bubble Tea, the Miso Ramen, Prawn Crackers and Acocado-Salmon Hosimaki Sushi.\n\nMy personal favorite was the Ramen with Chilli Oil drizzle. They do have chopsticks if you don't see one please ask them.\n\nThank you Kevin and team for timely serving of food and your kind behavior. That added more to the ambience.\n\nWill visit again.",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              }
            ],
