            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "Aparajita Ekka",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Really enjoyed the food here! The Pambazo and Churros were the highlights—both were absolutely delicious. We also tried the tacos, nachos, and quesadillas, which were great. Loved that most dishes have customizable non-veg options. Definitely worth a visit!",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Poushalee Dey",
                "rating": 3,
                "text": "We dropped by Chinita Real Mexican Food in Koramangala for a relaxed Saturday afternoon lunch, a spot well known in Bengaluru for bringing relatively authentic Mexican flavours to the city. The restaurant has a casual, colourful vibe with an easygoing café energy that works perfectly for slow weekend meals.\nWe began with the Margarita De Tamarindo, a tamarind-based margarita featuring tamarind pulp, lime juice, and a chilli-salt rim. The drink was tangy, refreshing, and slightly adventurous—the tamarind added a pleasant sweet-sour depth, while the chilli salt provided a nice kick that lingered after each sip.\nFor food, we ordered the Grilled Tacos with Chicken Tinga, a classic Mexican preparation where shredded chicken is cooked in a smoky tomato-chipotle style sauce. The tacos were flavourful and comforting, with soft tortillas holding well-seasoned chicken that delivered gentle heat without overpowering the palate.\nThe Burrito Bowl with Grilled Chicken followed—cilantro rice layered with beans, cheese, salsa, onions, sour cream, jalapeños, and green peppers. It was hearty and filling, leaning toward familiar comfort food rather than bold complexity. The grilled chicken added protein and texture, though the flavours overall felt safe rather than standout.\nWe wrapped up the meal with a Flan for dessert. Smooth, custardy, and lightly caramelised, it was a pleasant finish—silky in texture and not overly sweet, making it a satisfying way to close the meal.\nService was relaxed and matched the laid-back atmosphere, though the experience overall landed somewhere between enjoyable and memorable. The food was good, the flavours approachable, and the ambience inviting—but nothing quite reached the “wow” factor.",
                "published": "6 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "SAURABH INDORIA",
                "rating": 3,
                "text": "This is certainly not Mexican food. I've tried many places in the US, and trying to find something similar in India. This place is not it. Guacamole was out of stock, from a Mexican restaurant, stating it is out of season, was a big disappointment. The beans used are with Rajma masala of India, not the roasted beans like it is used in actual Mexican food. Taco shells are different than the original Mexican ones. Price is super high, in some cases, it was higher than what you get in US as well, even with the dollar conversion. It might be a good place to try, but definitely not an authentic mexican restaurant.",
                "published": "6 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Abhilash Thakur",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "We were here yesterday for dinner.\nAmbiance is simple, nothing elaborate. They have painted walls and bulbs hanging from the ceiling.\nWe had their Mushroom and Spinach Enchiladas and Prawns Grilled Tacos.\nThe Enchiladas was rich, creamy and tasted good. It had stuffed tacos baked with tomato salsa, topped with molten cheese, Mushroom and spinach.\nThe grilled tacos was crispy, loaded with cheese, onion tomato sauce and Prawns. It tasted good too.\nService was quick, prices are slightly high. Overall, a good experience",
                "published": "a month ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Rangana Sarkar",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Tried Chinita in Koramangla I visited recently and had a really good experience. I ordered tacos, burrito and a rice bowl all of them were filling. The tacos had nice flavour, the burrito was wholesome and the rice bowl was well balanced and fresh. Portions were good too For dessert, I had churros and they were the highlight perfectly sweet. Overall, really enjoyed the food and the vibe. Definitely a place  I would visit again",
                "published": "5 months ago"
              }
            ],
