            "phone": "072592 32851",
            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "Shashank Ananthoju",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "I've visited Pasta Street in Koramangala twice now, and both visits were enjoyable. On my first visit, we tried the Arrabbiata Salad and Roma Chilli Garlic Pasta, and both were flavorful and well prepared.\n\nOn my second visit, I tried the Crema Monte, and it was just as good. The pasta was creamy, satisfying, and cooked perfectly.\n\nOverall, it's a nice place if you're craving Italian food. The quality has been consistent across both visits, and I'd definitely come back to try more from their menu.",
                "published": "2 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Kumar Ankit",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "If you’re looking for a slice of Italy tucked into Bangalore’s buzzing food scene, Pasta Street Koramangala delivers a dining experience that’s both comforting and quietly refined.\nFrom the moment you step in, the ambience sets the tone—warm lighting, rustic wooden accents, and a laid-back European café vibe that invites you to slow down. It’s the kind of place where conversations linger as long as the food does.\nThe menu is a celebration of authentic Italian flavors without feeling overwhelming. What stands out immediately is their commitment to freshness—especially with their pasta, which is often made in-house. Each dish feels thoughtfully crafted rather than mass-produced. The sauces strike a beautiful balance: rich but not heavy, flavorful yet not overpowering.\nThe pasta, of course, is the star. Whether you go for a creamy Alfredo or a tangy tomato-based option, the texture is perfectly al dente, and the ingredients shine through with clarity. Their wood-fired pizzas deserve a mention too—thin crust, slightly charred edges, and a topping combination that feels both classic and satisfying.\nService here complements the experience well—attentive without being intrusive, and genuinely warm. It adds to the overall charm of the place.\nWhat makes Pasta Street truly stand out is consistency. It doesn’t try to reinvent Italian cuisine—it respects it. And in doing so, it creates a space you’d want to return to, whether for a casual lunch, a date night, or a quiet solo meal.\nVerdict: A reliable go-to for quality Italian food in Koramangala, where good food meets great ambience.",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Vindhya Gowda",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Pasta Street, as the name suggests, serves some really tasty pastas and the quality of food is consistently good. My all-time favorite is the chicken white sauce pasta—it’s absolutely delicious. The drinks are great too, and the chicken wings are lip-smacking.\n\nThe pastas are quite addictive, and they have an open kitchen, which makes the place feel clean and well-maintained. Service is good and efficient. It is a bit on the expensive side, but definitely worth it for the quality and taste.",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Hema malini",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "The pasta here is simply excellent. I tried one with the combination of white red and pesto. Have not had anything like this and loved it!\n\nWe also tried the rose sangria and it was mindblowing and super refreshing!\n\nThe dessert selection was not that great but plays a good supporting cast.\n\nAll in all, a good place for really really good pasta. Lives up to the hype.",
                "published": "5 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Josef Mathew",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "I really liked this place! The service and ambience were top notch. The food was really good with the fettuccine pasta, veggie salad and garlic bread being my favorites. Tomato soup and pizza seemed very average but overall, good place to try italian cuisine.",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              }
            ],
