                "reviews": [
                  {
                    "author": "p. pat",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": "The Chinese restaurant is located on the 3rd floor of the Shangri-La Hotel. I went there mainly to try the Peking duck and the hotpot.\nIf you order the hotpot, you’ll need to sit at the outdoor seating area. The food took quite a while to arrive around 30 minutes before the first dish came out.\nThe Peking duck was tasty overall, though the skin wasn’t as crispy as I expected. The fried rice was surprisingly good and definitely one of the better dishes of the meal.\nFor the hotpot, we ordered the Sichuan spicy broth, but the flavor was quite mild. It felt like the taste had been adjusted to suit Indian preferences, so it lacked the numbing, spicy kick you’d normally expect from authentic Sichuan broth. The dipping sauces were okay, but nothing particularly memorable.\nService was generally good, although they made billing mistakes a few times\n\nI’d probably come back again.",
                    "published": "3 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "C W",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "As a Taiwanese, I’m confident to say the food was authentic and incredibly delicious – a solid 10/10.  Banitha’s service was top-notch and the Swiggy offer made the dinner even more value for money. We’ll definitely be back soon!",
                    "published": "5 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "Harsha",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "Review police who say vegetarian and Chinese food don't go hand in hand avoid reading.\n\nThere are restaurants that serve vegetarian Chinese food, and then there is Shang Palace a place that actually understands it.\n\nTried the five-course vegetarian sampling menu, dim-sums and tofu dishes(Sichuan pepper tofu and Mapo Tofu) are brilliant, FYI nothing is altered for the sake of pandering to an Indian palette, it's authentic Guangdong and Sichuan cuisine and that's the brilliance of the place.\n\nThe homemade ice cream lineup is genuinely inventive; the black sesame and goji berry is not to be missed.The service is unhurried without being slow\n\nIdeally the serving size for this sampling menu is for 2 people but go in hungry on a weekend and make it your only meal for the day.",
                    "published": "3 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "Prashant Chhetri",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "Visit sang palace for the first time and I was really happy with the ambience the staff was really good and friendly mostly Miss Shalma,Miss Neha , Miss Roshina and lastly Mr Adarsh they help me with everything from the time I enterd the premises keep it up guys.\nThe food was really on a top notch really appreciate definitely comming back for the vibe and the friendly staff",
                    "published": "2 months ago"
                  },
                  {
                    "author": "D",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": "This restaurant and the one at the Ritz are my go-to Chinese restaurants in Bangalore. I love the tofu chili starter. Mapo tofu is also quite good. Negative: Beer prices are absolutely overpriced. 7 dollars for a small bottle is ridiculously for Bangalore.",
                    "published": "10 months ago"
                  }
                ],
