            "reviews": [
              {
                "author": "Neil Whitcher",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Went for Sunday lunch, great to get out of the old town for a proper sit down meal, staff were amazing, relaxed service with families and locals… every dish was delicious, Aspargus, , Arroz to start… monkfish and then the steak all amazing, great place",
                "published": "3 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Benjamin T P Tan (btptan)",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Nicely away from the busy areas.\nWe went with the chef's specialty - the Monkfish. Came out to be 1.5kg. Good size for 2 to share. Perhaps 3 or 4 if you're having lots of other stuff. Note that price on the menu is per kg. Spot on timing for the texture. Good balance of garlic and lemon. Would have liked a touch more of the chilli/pepper but that's my usual bias. I wonder what happened to the monkfish Liver! Also, compliments to the waiter who carved in the fish expertly.\n\nWe also had the small portion of the seafood paella. The slightly sweetish flavour was very agreeable to me. Only minor grumble (maybe I should have requested explicitly) is that more socarrat would have been welcomed! For the 2 of us (not particularly small eaters), this and the monkish was great but that left no space remaining for the cheesecake.\n\nSangria was a particularly good blend. Yes, everyone/every bar seems to have their own variant, that's fine. We enjoyed This variant!\n\nThe house white suggested by the waiter to go with the monkfish paired well.\n\nI think price is fair for this quality. Would return without hesitation. Even perhaps later tonight for the the cheesecake...",
                "published": "10 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "David",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "The perfect neighbourhood restaurant. We spent a glorious few hours here with our one year old and were treated to fantastic food and friendly service. Highly recommended - particularly the monkfish.",
                "published": "4 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Kevin Monaghan",
                "rating": 5,
                "text": "Small and unassuming but this place packs a punch. Just loved it. Had a terrific Rioja and chef gifted us a pintxo of Lomo on Toast. Had the Tomato Salad with Sliced Onions and Ventresca Tuna Belly followed by Stuffed Peppers with Beef Cheeks and their famous Cheesecake. Wow!!!",
                "published": "7 months ago"
              },
              {
                "author": "Fei Fei Metzler",
                "rating": 4,
                "text": "Nice little restaurant. Unassuming in appearances. Good food and service. A place clearly visited by locals. For starters we shared Jamon Iberico. Good quantity and excellent flavors. For entrees, the three of us shared monkfish and grilled octopus. Broth were great. The octopus was tender with brunt crunchy bits. Mashed potato towers were pretty and tasty. The monkfish in this region is the best. Simply prepared with garlic and lemon. The fish is tender and flavorful. The bed of thin potato rounds are perfectly done. Buttery soft but still has integrity.  To finish off the meal, we shared a cheesecake. The best of the Basque style that I have had. Everything was great.",
                "published": "11 months ago"
              }
            ],
